      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:pulse_cairn",
      "text": [
        "A cairn of stones that holds a beat. Each stone stores **4,000 Pulse** and drinks the surplus of nearby generators, up to **200 a second**. Bursty generators fill it; hungry machines draw on it steadily."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Piling",
      "text": [
        "Cairns that touch face to face, on any side, above or below, join into **one pile** and one store: two stones hold **8,000 Pulse**, three hold **12,000**, and so on. A pile joins up to **64 stones**, which is **256,000 Pulse**; a stone past that stands alone.",
        "Use any stone and you see the whole pile. Put Pulse in anywhere and it spreads across the stones; draw from any stone and the whole pile pays. Each stone adds 200 a second to how fast the pile drinks.",
        "A cairn only pulls from **generators** within 8 blocks of its stones, never from another cairn. Machines within 8 blocks spend generators first, then cairns.",
        "Break a stone and it takes only its own share with it; the rest of the pile keeps what it holds.",
        "A comparator against any stone reads how full the whole pile is. A redstone signal on any stone stops the pile filling."
      ]
    },
